# tinnas.ref  --  reference / contract data for test/init/tinnas.f
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Purpose: documents the expected behaviour of modern/init/nastinit.f,
#          the single initialisation entry point invoked once from the
#          bootstrap by 'CALL NASTINIT' (inserted immediately after
#          CALL DBMINT in bin/nastrn.f).
#
# Contract under test (assumed cross-agent interface):
#   SUBROUTINE NASTINIT            ! no arguments
#     Reads NASTRAN_LEGACY_INIT via GETENV and orchestrates the explicit
#     init path (diagctl + blkinit [+ initval]) invoked exactly once.
#
# Toggle semantics (ASSUMED; flagged for maintainer confirmation):
#   NASTRAN_LEGACY_INIT unset (default) -> modern explicit init path;
#                                          NASTINIT calls BLKINIT so the
#                                          COMMON state is populated.
#   NASTRAN_LEGACY_INIT set             -> legacy load-time path (the 39
#                                          bd/ BLOCK DATA units), proven
#                                          equivalent by the regression
#                                          harness, not by this driver.
#
# Format:  comment lines begin with '#'; data lines are 'KEY VALUE'.
# Run with NASTRAN_INIT_VALIDATE=1 and NASTRAN_LEGACY_INIT unset.
# EXPECT_VERDICT PASS: TINNAS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Binding assertions consumed by tinnas.f (default / modern path):
#   EXPDIV = 0 -> after CALL NASTINIT the init state validates with zero
#                 divergence (NASTINIT correctly orchestrated blkinit).
#   EXPRAN = 1 -> the post-check validator actually executed.
EXPDIV 0
EXPRAN 1
# end of tinnas.ref
